Subject: Cantor Provider-Free Self-Work Composition P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] d6a870c5-946c-4c49-91c3-d4aed60c1aa5
@ [canonical_uuid] d36ead3a-82eb-4a88-897e-1d903cc01c01

& [WhyNow]
  + SWA-01 through SWA-04A and SWA-06A are published but still appear as separate seams to product recall
  + the smallest next proof is that their exact supplied forms compose causally without changing or activating them

& [WhyThisShape]
  + lifecycle equality prevents unrelated boot plan and objective chains from being spliced
  + exact transition prefix preserves temporal custody between the handoff and next-SOP checkpoints
  + exact propose_update and propose_succeeding_sop classes prevent generic ready-step laundering
  + attempt continuity completion and bridge evidence bind the update intent into the later causal record
  + full downstream recompilation and wrapper digests make the receipt self-contained and independently replayable

& [WhyEcosystem]
  + cantor_ecosystem already owns the SWA-04A handoff and depends on cantor_core which owns every other required pure form
  + this avoids dependency inversion or modification of stable predecessor modules

& [Nonclaims]
  + integration correspondence is not work execution update verification publication semantic review signature activation provider readiness or an autonomous product
